{title: 529 - Under His Wings}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #529 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 529}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/G]Under [Am]Hiswings [C]I am [F/C]safely [G7]abiding;
[G7]Though the night deepens [C/G]and tempests [Am]are [C]wild,
[C]Still I cantrust [F/C]Him; [C]I [Bdim]know [Am]He [C/G]will keep [G]me;
[G7/F]He has [C/E]redeemed me, and I am [G]His [Dm]child.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G/D]Under [C/G]His wings, under His [F/C]wings,
[C]Who from His [G]love [C/E]can sever?
[C]Under [Am]His wings, [C]my [F/C]soul [G]shall [C/G]abide,
[C/G]Safely abide [Dm/F]forever.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/G]Under [Am]His [C]wings, what a refuge [G7]in [C/G]sorrow!
[G7]How the heart yearningly [C/G]turns [G7]to [Am]its [C]rest!
[C]Often when [F/C]earth has [C]no [Bdim]balm [Am]for [C/G]my healing,
[G7/F]There I [C/E]find comfort, and there I [G]am [Dm]blest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/G]Under [Am]His [C]wings, O what precious [G7]enjoyment!
[G7]There will I hide till life's [C/G]trials [G7]are [Am]over;
[C]Sheltered, protected, no [Bdim]evil [C/G]can harm [G]me;
[G7/F]Resting [C/E]in Jesus I'm safe evermore.
{end_of_verse}
